      "card_ids": ["C46","C50","C19","C184","C161"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 doxycycline Caco-2 records show A-B Papp of 3.4 ± 0.23 ×10^-6 cm/s and an efflux ratio of 1.2, indicating that the tetracycline class can exhibit good permeability and minimal P-gp efflux.",
      "card_ids": ["C290","C257","C260"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 tetracycline P-gp substrate and mucin-barrier records are class-level mechanistic concerns, but tetracycline itself has high human oral bioavailability; they are not affirmative evidence that the query fluorocycline has F<20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C249","C284","C292","C250"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No direct eravacycline-specific absolute oral bioavailability, permeability, or efflux record is supplied; the high prediction rests on class-level transfer and means F≥20% is better supported, not that a specific F value or formulation is established.",
